[00:01.50]From the information given in the pie chart,
[00:04.82]we can see the survey on the reasons for starting 
[00:07.82]one’s own business among college students in a certain university.
[00:13.54]Those whose ideals are to become entrepreneurs account for 44%,
[00:18.39]the biggest among all the five categories,
[00:21.63]while those who could not find suitable jobs account for 15%.
[00:26.21]As long as they are cautious,
[00:28.37]this kind of real-world experience can greatly benefit 
[00:31.37]their future careers.
[00:34.30]Above all,
[00:35.11]students who launch their own businesses can gain 
[00:38.11]valuable insight into their future career path.
[00:42.57]Some students may even choose to switch majors as a result of 
[00:45.57]insight gained from entrepreneurial activities.
[00:50.93]In addition,
[00:51.91]regardless of whether a student succeeds or fails in a business venture,
[00:54.40]the mere fact of having work experience will come in handy 
[00:58.40]when seeking a full-time job after graduation.
[01:02.31]Employers will regard these students as more ambitious,
[01:06.62]hard-working and mature than graduates who lack such work experience.
[01:12.01]Despite the benefits to students of “getting their feet wet” 
[01:16.01]in the business world,
[01:17.30]it is crucial that they maintain academic studies as a top priority.
[ti:2-05-创业]